# V4 GARCH — Duan LRNVR

When editing files under `V4-Models_result/garch notebook/`:

- Estimate Duan GARCH-in-mean \((\lambda,\omega,\alpha,\beta,\sigma_0)\) from lookback returns and observed DGS3MO \(r_{f,t}\). \(\lambda\) is the **unit risk premium**, not a jump intensity.
- Do **not** add Merton jump parameters \(\lambda_J,\mu_J,\sigma_J,\kappa\).
- Do **not** risk-neutralize by replacing \(\mu\to r\) only. §6 LSM must use Duan LRNVR \(Q\)-paths: mean \(r_f-\tfrac12\sigma_t^2\), variance shock \((\xi_t-\lambda)\).
- \(\omega,\alpha,\beta,\lambda,\sigma_0\) are the same numbers under \(Q\); only the mean and the GARCH innovation change.
- Shared implementation: `V4-Models_result/scripts/garch_duan_lrnvr.py`.
- True rolling-window calibration (daily / monthly / none) still applies.
- §4 graphs: \(\lambda,\omega,\alpha,\beta,\sigma_0\), plus separate P vs Q tables after Reestimate.
- See `V4-Models_result/garch notebook/ROLLING_CALIBRATION.md` and `V4_CHANGES.md`.
